 "result_text": "I fixed the crash in `manage_addZSearch` in `src/Shared/DC/ZRDB/Search.py`. I haven't run it or any tests, so the fix is untested.\n\nThe cause was `qs = map(...)` on line 47. On Python 3, `map` returns an iterator, so the later `len(qs)` raised `TypeError: object of type 'map' has no len()`. I replaced it with a list comprehension: `qs = [_getquery(self, q) for q in queries]`.\n\nI checked the other `map` calls in the file. Two sit inside `'\\n'.join(...)` in the default input form builders, and the others are only passed to `join`. None of them need `len()` or a second pass, so I left them alone.\n\nI only read through `manage_addZSearch` as far as the DTML report branch (up to line 90). The ZPT branch and the rest of the search path could still have other Python 3 problems.",
